Suddenly, a dog barks loudly.
My family laughs.
My father lifts Lola up.
He holds Lola right in front of the camera.
I laugh too.
"Hello Lola!" I call.
Lola looks into the laptop.
She is a very good dog.
"Who is a good dog?" I ask.
Lola barks once more.
My sister Sofia pets her.
"Who is walking Lola now?" I ask my family.
Normally, that is my job.
"Your brother walks her every day," my mother says.
My brother Diego nods proudly.
"Yes, Lola and I are a good team," he says.
I am very glad about that.
I miss Lola a lot.
